00:02:34.530 --> 00:02:36.637
Let's dive back into how
Europe stole the world.

00:02:36.637 --> 00:02:38.100
(upbeat music)

00:02:38.100 --> 00:02:40.110
Okay, quick catch-up on
where we are in the story.

00:02:40.110 --> 00:02:42.150
In part one, we talked
about how Spain and Portugal

00:02:42.150 --> 00:02:43.740
went out to get in on trade

00:02:43.740 --> 00:02:45.630
and accidentally ran into a bunch of land

00:02:45.630 --> 00:02:48.480
they decided was unclaimed,
and it turned into a big race

00:02:48.480 --> 00:02:50.790
to see who could take over
as much land as possible.

00:02:50.790 --> 00:02:52.680
After about a century of this,

00:02:52.680 --> 00:02:54.630
other Europeans start to take notice

00:02:54.630 --> 00:02:56.763
of this model of expansion,

00:02:58.080 --> 00:02:59.550
and they realize that it's a a great way

00:02:59.550 --> 00:03:00.990
to enrich your country.

00:03:00.990 --> 00:03:03.180
Some of these countries have
been dabbling in imperialism,

00:03:03.180 --> 00:03:06.900
but in the early 1600s it
was time to get serious.

00:03:06.900 --> 00:03:09.000
The first to follow suit were the Dutch

00:03:09.000 --> 00:03:11.730
who were becoming really
good at navigating water

00:03:11.730 --> 00:03:14.220
and making maps and doing business.

00:03:14.220 --> 00:03:15.960
They decided to follow Portugal's lead

00:03:15.960 --> 00:03:17.850
and go around the bottom of Africa,

00:03:17.850 --> 00:03:19.740
stopping right here at the very tip

00:03:19.740 --> 00:03:22.710
in what today is known as
Cape Town, South Africa.

00:03:22.710 --> 00:03:25.290
They established a permanent
colony of white settlers

00:03:25.290 --> 00:03:26.670
whose descendants would go on

00:03:26.670 --> 00:03:29.811
to become a major part of
South Africa's history.

00:03:29.811 --> 00:03:31.550
(images whooshing)

00:03:31.550 --> 00:03:34.300
(cheerful music)

00:03:35.370 --> 00:03:37.500
The Dutch used their prime
position in Cape Town

00:03:37.500 --> 00:03:40.080
to restock on their way to Southeast Asia

00:03:40.080 --> 00:03:43.350
where they were trading for
spices with local empires

00:03:43.350 --> 00:03:45.480
and claiming serious amounts of land

00:03:45.480 --> 00:03:47.550
in what is today in Indonesia.

00:03:47.550 --> 00:03:49.890
Around the same time, at
the start of the 1600s,

00:03:49.890 --> 00:03:52.290
we see the next kingdoms trying their hand

00:03:52.290 --> 00:03:54.420
at large scale imperialism.

00:03:54.420 --> 00:03:56.668
Meet the two rookies on the block,

00:03:56.668 --> 00:03:58.830
(upbeat music)

00:03:58.830 --> 00:04:01.080
England and France, who would go on

00:04:01.080 --> 00:04:03.390
to actually cause a lot of
trouble on the world map,

00:04:03.390 --> 00:04:04.890
but for now they're just getting started.

00:04:04.890 --> 00:04:07.170
They, for the most part,
followed Spain's lead

00:04:07.170 --> 00:04:08.910
going west for the Americas,

00:04:08.910 --> 00:04:11.490
though England sent ships
east at this time as well.

00:04:11.490 --> 00:04:13.680
Anyway, here in the
Americas they showed up

00:04:13.680 --> 00:04:16.680
and, like colonizers before
them, found lots of land

00:04:16.680 --> 00:04:19.260
and lots of people living on that land.

00:04:19.260 --> 00:04:20.377
Hm, kind of inconvenient.

00:04:20.377 --> 00:04:22.777
"These aren't real people, right?

00:04:22.777 --> 00:04:25.080
"They don't actually own this land,"

00:04:25.080 --> 00:04:26.370
you can hear the English people

00:04:26.370 --> 00:04:28.290
like sort of saying to themselves.

00:04:28.290 --> 00:04:30.930
So they came up with a
new very useful tool.

00:04:30.930 --> 00:04:32.220
It was a mental tool.

00:04:32.220 --> 00:04:34.710
In addition to guns and smallpox

00:04:34.710 --> 00:04:36.270
and alliances with local tribes

00:04:36.270 --> 00:04:38.220
that helped them divide
and conquer the locals,

00:04:38.220 --> 00:04:41.880
Europeans also developed a
complex set of legal philosophies

00:04:41.880 --> 00:04:42.960
to convince themselves

00:04:42.960 --> 00:04:45.510
that these people were not in fact capable

00:04:45.510 --> 00:04:46.920
to claim any land.

00:04:46.920 --> 00:04:49.020
After all, they were foragers.

00:04:49.020 --> 00:04:50.280
They didn't farm.

00:04:50.280 --> 00:04:51.420
They couldn't own this land

00:04:51.420 --> 00:04:53.580
because they didn't use
it for productive means.

00:04:53.580 --> 00:04:56.340
They were subhuman, or
at least non-civilized,

00:04:56.340 --> 00:04:58.860
so they do not deserve to own property.

00:04:58.860 --> 00:05:01.171
Very clever, very effective.

00:05:01.171 --> 00:05:03.840
(upbeat music)

00:05:03.840 --> 00:05:07.920
And so now you see the next
layer of ideological thinking

00:05:07.920 --> 00:05:10.320
that was required for these Europeans

00:05:10.320 --> 00:05:12.240
to justify their land theft.

00:05:12.240 --> 00:05:13.980
It was the need to dehumanize

00:05:13.980 --> 00:05:15.971
the people living on these lands.

00:05:15.971 --> 00:05:18.554
(upbeat music)

00:05:21.360 --> 00:05:23.430
Here's a letter from a British settler

00:05:23.430 --> 00:05:26.437
who describes North America
as a wilderness, quote,

00:05:26.437 --> 00:05:30.780
"Where none inhabit but hellish
fiends and brutish men."

00:05:30.780 --> 00:05:34.080
This dehumanizing paired really
well with another ideology

00:05:34.080 --> 00:05:36.938
that was very popular at
the time, Christianity,

00:05:36.938 --> 00:05:37.771
(angelic music)

00:05:37.771 --> 00:05:39.840
a religion that told
its followers to go out

00:05:39.840 --> 00:05:43.320
and preach to everyone so
that they can be saved.

00:05:43.320 --> 00:05:44.359
Perfect.

00:05:44.359 --> 00:05:49.359
(birds cawing)
(upbeat music)

00:05:51.720 --> 00:05:54.210
We have these unrefined,
brutish, fiendish men,

00:05:54.210 --> 00:05:56.850
and we have Christians who
have the power to save them.

00:05:56.850 --> 00:05:58.230
Anything is possible now.

00:05:58.230 --> 00:05:59.610
So by the late 1600s,

00:05:59.610 --> 00:06:02.250
the colonizing project is fully underway.

00:06:02.250 --> 00:06:03.630
A lot of Europeans are getting in on this,

00:06:03.630 --> 00:06:05.040
but here are the major players.

00:06:05.040 --> 00:06:07.470
You've got Spain and Portugal, the OGs,

00:06:07.470 --> 00:06:10.710
and then you've got the
Netherlands, France, and England.

00:06:10.710 --> 00:06:11.700
We need to make one thing clear

00:06:11.700 --> 00:06:14.310
that the major reason why
these European empires

00:06:14.310 --> 00:06:16.110
were so successful so quickly

00:06:16.110 --> 00:06:18.480
was because they were really the first

00:06:18.480 --> 00:06:21.060
to start trading by sea
in the Western Hemisphere.

00:06:21.060 --> 00:06:23.460
So while Jesus and saving and whatever

00:06:23.460 --> 00:06:25.590
was a big part of the justification

00:06:25.590 --> 00:06:28.890
of Europeans going out and
feeling entitled to take land,

00:06:28.890 --> 00:06:32.430
he became less and less
of a part of the picture,

00:06:32.430 --> 00:06:34.987
especially for the Dutch who
basically were just like,

00:06:34.987 --> 00:06:37.197
"Who cares about Jesus? We want profit."

00:06:37.197 --> 00:06:40.290
(cheerful music)

00:06:40.290 --> 00:06:42.000
And this is the next phase of the story

00:06:42.000 --> 00:06:44.130
of how Europe took over the world.

00:06:44.130 --> 00:06:46.800
We'll call this chapter Private Empire,

00:06:46.800 --> 00:06:48.960
and frankly, it's one of
the most important things

00:06:48.960 --> 00:06:50.481
to know about this history.

00:06:50.481 --> 00:06:52.830
(cheerful music)

00:06:52.830 --> 00:06:55.230
Remember that European imperialism started

00:06:55.230 --> 00:06:56.640
as a desire for trade,

00:06:56.640 --> 00:06:58.290
to trade with big empires in the east.

00:06:58.290 --> 00:07:00.120
Then surprise, we found all this land.

00:07:00.120 --> 00:07:01.890
We'll call it unclaimed
and we'll start claiming it

00:07:01.890 --> 00:07:03.540
while dehumanizing the
natives in the process.

00:07:03.540 --> 00:07:04.710
Remember? Okay.

00:07:04.710 --> 00:07:07.980
A lot of that was funded by governments,

00:07:07.980 --> 00:07:09.240
like kings and stuff,

00:07:09.240 --> 00:07:12.300
but eventually the citizens
themselves of these places

00:07:12.300 --> 00:07:14.460
realized that they could
make a business out of this.

00:07:14.460 --> 00:07:17.648
And again, this is where the
Dutch wrote the blueprint.

00:07:17.648 --> 00:07:20.100
(cheerful music)

00:07:20.100 --> 00:07:23.010
So now instead of asking
the ruler for support,

00:07:23.010 --> 00:07:25.470
they could just get
together a bunch of people

00:07:25.470 --> 00:07:29.070
and form a corporation, like
the first corporation ever,

00:07:29.070 --> 00:07:30.870
the Dutch East India Company,

00:07:30.870 --> 00:07:33.000
which would fund private voyages.

00:07:33.000 --> 00:07:35.670
And you, a random Dutch
person in the 1600s,

00:07:35.670 --> 00:07:39.120
could buy this share, a little
portion of that company,

00:07:39.120 --> 00:07:41.190
to get in on a little bit of the profits.

00:07:41.190 --> 00:07:44.070
But if the profits are big
enough, then everyone wins.

00:07:44.070 --> 00:07:46.882
Welcome to the era of corporations.

00:07:46.882 --> 00:07:48.660
(energetic music)

00:07:48.660 --> 00:07:49.493
So now you have the Dutch

00:07:49.493 --> 00:07:51.120
with their new Kickstarter campaign

00:07:51.120 --> 00:07:53.250
crowdfunding their private empire,

00:07:53.250 --> 00:07:54.870
totally exceeding their goal.

00:07:54.870 --> 00:07:56.730
And these Dutch corporate sailors set out

00:07:56.730 --> 00:07:59.610
on the tried and true routes
that they already knew,

00:07:59.610 --> 00:08:02.160
arriving to Indonesia where they showed up

00:08:02.160 --> 00:08:04.950
not to convert people
to Jesus necessarily,

00:08:04.950 --> 00:08:08.310
but to harvest cloves and peppers
as efficiently as possible

00:08:08.310 --> 00:08:10.710
and to come home and to
sell them for a profit

00:08:10.710 --> 00:08:13.380
and fatten the pockets of the shareholders

00:08:13.380 --> 00:08:14.790
who funded the whole journey.

00:08:14.790 --> 00:08:17.430
This isn't like a surprising
novel model to us today

00:08:17.430 --> 00:08:19.320
because this is how the world runs,

00:08:19.320 --> 00:08:21.690
but at this point, this
was a new invention.

00:08:21.690 --> 00:08:23.490
Oh, and the government
secretly loved this.

00:08:23.490 --> 00:08:25.740
They could give the company
some military power,

00:08:25.740 --> 00:08:26.820
kind of ignore the details

00:08:26.820 --> 00:08:28.650
of exactly how it was all going down,

00:08:28.650 --> 00:08:30.570
and still ensure that their country got in

00:08:30.570 --> 00:08:31.860
on the world's riches.

00:08:31.860 --> 00:08:34.200
And these corporations
leveled up really quickly

00:08:34.200 --> 00:08:36.720
and became basically
little private empires

00:08:36.720 --> 00:08:39.900
with the ability to take
over land, build bases,

00:08:39.900 --> 00:08:41.880
and establish relationships with locals,

00:08:41.880 --> 00:08:43.920
not for the prestige of like a king,

00:08:43.920 --> 00:08:45.750
but so that they could make more money

00:08:45.750 --> 00:08:46.860
for their shareholders.

00:08:46.860 --> 00:08:48.300
It was the private investors

00:08:48.300 --> 00:08:50.910
who helped them get really big really fast

00:08:50.910 --> 00:08:54.645
all through this invention of
the publicly traded company.

00:08:54.645 --> 00:08:58.170
(melancholy music)

00:08:58.170 --> 00:09:00.750
And again, it all started with
the Dutch East India Company.

00:09:00.750 --> 00:09:01.920
And just like any startup,

00:09:01.920 --> 00:09:05.040
they were more nimble than
the clunky old government.

00:09:05.040 --> 00:09:06.090
They had good funding.

00:09:06.090 --> 00:09:08.250
They were private. They were fast.

00:09:08.250 --> 00:09:10.350
They had an ability to
undercut competition.

00:09:10.350 --> 00:09:13.620
All of this allowed them
to dominate this region

00:09:13.620 --> 00:09:16.950
when it came to taking over
land, harvesting stuff,

00:09:16.950 --> 00:09:18.210
and bringing it back to Europe.

00:09:18.210 --> 00:09:20.190
And because they were the best operators,

00:09:20.190 --> 00:09:21.990
they eventually became the kingpins

00:09:21.990 --> 00:09:24.060
of all spice trade in Europe,

00:09:24.060 --> 00:09:26.040
things like black pepper, nutmeg, cloves,

00:09:26.040 --> 00:09:28.170
all of this because of the countless trips

00:09:28.170 --> 00:09:31.289
that they were taking between
the East Indies and Amsterdam.

00:09:31.289 --> 00:09:36.030
(melancholy music)
(thunder cracking)

00:09:36.030 --> 00:09:37.320
Okay, but it wasn't just the Dutch,

00:09:37.320 --> 00:09:41.036
the British also got in on
this private empire idea.

00:09:41.036 --> 00:09:43.620
(dramatic music)

00:09:43.620 --> 00:09:44.700
Let's see here.

00:09:44.700 --> 00:09:46.260
This map, it's the map

00:09:46.260 --> 00:09:49.020
of all of the British private companies

00:09:49.020 --> 00:09:50.640
and there's spheres of influence.

00:09:50.640 --> 00:09:52.110
The government doesn't own these places.

00:09:52.110 --> 00:09:53.700
This is like government-supported

00:09:53.700 --> 00:09:55.920
but by and large private companies,

00:09:55.920 --> 00:09:57.990
profit-seeking businessmen
looking for stuff

00:09:57.990 --> 00:09:59.610
that they couldn't get
in their own country

00:09:59.610 --> 00:10:01.890
going out and finding
places where they could.

00:10:01.890 --> 00:10:04.170
Over here in North America
you have the Virginia Company

00:10:04.170 --> 00:10:05.970
who's like going hardcore on tobacco,

00:10:05.970 --> 00:10:08.850
and then its sister company,
the Plymouth Company.

00:10:08.850 --> 00:10:11.370
One was funded by a bunch of Londoners

00:10:11.370 --> 00:10:13.650
and the other, the
Plymouth Company, funded

00:10:13.650 --> 00:10:16.440
by a bunch of rich dudes
in Plymouth, England.

00:10:16.440 --> 00:10:18.420
Their job was to colonize land

00:10:18.420 --> 00:10:20.700
and to build a business in the new world.

00:10:20.700 --> 00:10:22.290
And then if you look
over here in the east,

00:10:22.290 --> 00:10:24.210
you see the British East India Company

00:10:24.210 --> 00:10:25.320
who got really good

00:10:25.320 --> 00:10:28.696
at taking over giant
amounts of land in India.

00:10:28.696 --> 00:10:31.200
(dramatic music)

00:10:31.200 --> 00:10:33.090
The French were doing the same thing.

00:10:33.090 --> 00:10:35.340
They had their own West India Company

00:10:35.340 --> 00:10:36.600
that was colonizing the Caribbean

00:10:36.600 --> 00:10:39.868
to grow and sell sugar,
and many, many more.

00:10:39.868 --> 00:10:42.618
(dramatic music)

00:10:44.490 --> 00:10:48.630
Private empire was such a
powerful accelerant to imperialism

00:10:48.630 --> 00:10:50.460
because it got all of
these private empires

00:10:50.460 --> 00:10:51.780
to compete with each other

00:10:51.780 --> 00:10:53.640
and to get better and more efficient

00:10:53.640 --> 00:10:55.740
and to practice their conquests.

00:10:55.740 --> 00:10:58.620
Repetition fueled by
profit-seeking people.

00:10:58.620 --> 00:11:02.520
They developed amazing
skills and they drew maps,

00:11:02.520 --> 00:11:05.787
a lot of beautiful, beautiful maps.

00:11:05.787 --> 00:11:08.537
(dramatic music)

00:11:10.086 --> 00:11:13.200
As a map nerd, this is where
I start to, like, perk up.

00:11:13.200 --> 00:11:14.700
I notice around this time,

00:11:14.700 --> 00:11:17.610
like sort of late 1600s
and then the 1700s,

00:11:17.610 --> 00:11:20.520
European maps start to
fill out with more detail,

00:11:20.520 --> 00:11:21.810
with more accuracy.

00:11:21.810 --> 00:11:24.390
Because after all, the more
you can depict on paper,

00:11:24.390 --> 00:11:27.120
the better blueprint
you have to conquer land

00:11:27.120 --> 00:11:27.960
and exploit it.

00:11:27.960 --> 00:11:31.500
So by the 1700s, Europe
is now a different world

00:11:31.500 --> 00:11:33.360
than what you saw in the 1400s.

00:11:33.360 --> 00:11:36.270
You start to see kings
living in insane excess.

00:11:36.270 --> 00:11:38.910
Tea and coffee and chocolate
and tobacco and sugar,

00:11:38.910 --> 00:11:41.611
they have access to so much stuff.

00:11:41.611 --> 00:11:42.660
(dramatic music)

00:11:42.660 --> 00:11:44.130
And perhaps most significantly,

00:11:44.130 --> 00:11:45.600
it wasn't just for the ultra rich,

00:11:45.600 --> 00:11:47.280
it was a new middle class,

00:11:47.280 --> 00:11:50.040
the mercantile class of
merchants who were getting rich

00:11:50.040 --> 00:11:51.570
off of all of this new commerce.

00:11:51.570 --> 00:11:53.160
There was suddenly abundance.

00:11:53.160 --> 00:11:56.340
(dramatic music)

00:11:56.340 --> 00:11:58.320
And with abundance comes time,

00:11:58.320 --> 00:12:01.500
time to sit around and
think about art and science,

00:12:01.500 --> 00:12:04.650
all while sipping on coffee
harvested from faraway lands

00:12:04.650 --> 00:12:06.450
stimulating these European brains

00:12:06.450 --> 00:12:08.310
to invent new ways of measuring things,

00:12:08.310 --> 00:12:10.440
to observe the world, the stars,

00:12:10.440 --> 00:12:13.230
to manipulate nature, to make life better.

00:12:13.230 --> 00:12:16.860
And the competition between
these private empires just grew.

00:12:16.860 --> 00:12:18.900
And like with any
profit-seeking competition,

00:12:18.900 --> 00:12:21.450
these companies needed to keep leveling up

00:12:21.450 --> 00:12:23.790
how much wealth they could
extract from these places,

00:12:23.790 --> 00:12:27.180
how much land they could take
over to meet demand back home,

00:12:27.180 --> 00:12:29.130
until eventually they turned full on

00:12:29.130 --> 00:12:33.002
to the most horrific version
of profit-seeking imperialism:

00:12:33.002 --> 00:12:35.970
(dramatic music)

00:12:35.970 --> 00:12:38.340
stealing millions of people

00:12:38.340 --> 00:12:40.920
from most notably here in West Africa,

00:12:40.920 --> 00:12:44.843
taking them to their new colonies
and forcing them to work.

00:12:44.843 --> 00:12:46.405
(solemn music)

00:12:46.405 --> 00:12:49.405
(images screeching)

00:12:51.030 --> 00:12:53.850
Stealing and trading humans
and forcing them to work

00:12:53.850 --> 00:12:56.340
was not anything new to this continent.

00:12:56.340 --> 00:12:58.440
Islamic and African slave
traders had been doing this

00:12:58.440 --> 00:12:59.700
for a very long time,

00:12:59.700 --> 00:13:01.500
but it was here in the 1700s,

00:13:01.500 --> 00:13:03.420
in this context of private empire,

00:13:03.420 --> 00:13:05.160
that things really start to pick up

00:13:05.160 --> 00:13:06.630
as these European empires,

00:13:06.630 --> 00:13:09.990
mostly England, Portugal, and
France, took it to a new level

00:13:09.990 --> 00:13:12.270
to fuel their highly optimized,

00:13:12.270 --> 00:13:14.940
shareholder-fueled private empires.

00:13:14.940 --> 00:13:18.930
So optimized that the slave
trade itself was outsourced

00:13:18.930 --> 00:13:21.360
to a private company, at
least in the case of England.

00:13:21.360 --> 00:13:25.170
It was imperial profit-seeking
efficiency at its finest

00:13:25.170 --> 00:13:26.400
and most horrifying.

00:13:26.400 --> 00:13:28.650
You can almost hear the glee and greed

00:13:28.650 --> 00:13:32.257
in the voice of one English
slave trader who wrote, quote,

00:13:32.257 --> 00:13:35.737
"What a glorious and
advantageous trade this is.

00:13:35.737 --> 00:13:38.467
"It is the hinge on which all the trade

00:13:38.467 --> 00:13:39.868
"of this globe moves."

00:13:39.868 --> 00:13:42.510
(solemn music)

00:13:42.510 --> 00:13:44.730
But Europeans are starting
to become really enlightened

00:13:44.730 --> 00:13:45.840
at this point, right?

00:13:45.840 --> 00:13:48.660
Like, they're starting to
think through like human rights

00:13:48.660 --> 00:13:50.040
and like equality

00:13:50.040 --> 00:13:52.920
and starting to lay the
groundwork for like democracy.

00:13:52.920 --> 00:13:57.000
Yes, but remember that
these Europeans had ideas

00:13:57.000 --> 00:13:59.880
in their minds that were planted
hundreds of years earlier,

00:13:59.880 --> 00:14:03.180
ideas that allowed them to
invent things like the new world

00:14:03.180 --> 00:14:06.360
and unclaimed land that
actually belonged to them.

00:14:06.360 --> 00:14:09.300
They applied a lot of those
same ideas to the slave trade.

00:14:09.300 --> 00:14:10.530
A lack of Jesus,

00:14:10.530 --> 00:14:13.500
a lack of white European
culture and technology,

00:14:13.500 --> 00:14:17.490
making these people
inferior, in need of saviors,

00:14:17.490 --> 00:14:19.350
to make use of their land,

00:14:19.350 --> 00:14:22.204
their resources, and their bodies.

00:14:22.204 --> 00:14:24.954
(dramatic music)

00:14:28.780 --> 00:14:31.020
Okay, but let's just be clear
about what's happening here.

00:14:31.020 --> 00:14:32.130
Yes, this is about profit.

00:14:32.130 --> 00:14:33.570
Yes, this is about ideology.

00:14:33.570 --> 00:14:35.700
But this part is so damn important to me

00:14:35.700 --> 00:14:37.500
because this is the foundation

00:14:37.500 --> 00:14:40.110
upon which our modern world is built.

00:14:40.110 --> 00:14:43.020
In this moment, these empires
were actually building

00:14:43.020 --> 00:14:45.180
structures in our minds,

00:14:45.180 --> 00:14:47.700
structures that define who has power,

00:14:47.700 --> 00:14:50.850
who is worth something,
who gets resources,

00:14:50.850 --> 00:14:54.330
who is permitted to lead,
to exploit, to benefit.

00:14:54.330 --> 00:14:58.350
These structures were defined
by force, by profit, by greed,

00:14:58.350 --> 00:14:59.790
and they totally worked.

00:14:59.790 --> 00:15:01.230
They put Europeans on top,

00:15:01.230 --> 00:15:03.270
giving them the prosperity and resources

00:15:03.270 --> 00:15:06.990
to fuel scientific, cultural,
and political revolutions

00:15:06.990 --> 00:15:09.540
that allowed them to keep
holding onto that power,

00:15:09.540 --> 00:15:12.240
to keep exerting domination over others.

00:15:12.240 --> 00:15:13.170
Okay, yeah, I get it.

00:15:13.170 --> 00:15:14.940
Half of you just had like a conniption

00:15:14.940 --> 00:15:17.970
because of this like woke
sermon that you just got for me.

00:15:17.970 --> 00:15:19.440
That's not what this is, okay?

00:15:19.440 --> 00:15:22.710
I'm trying to look at the
history and tie it to today,

00:15:22.710 --> 00:15:24.990
how all of us live in a world

00:15:24.990 --> 00:15:27.810
that was built off of what
happened during this time,

00:15:27.810 --> 00:15:30.510
the ideas, the movement of people

00:15:30.510 --> 00:15:32.820
that happened because
of this private empire.

00:15:32.820 --> 00:15:33.840
That's not the woke mob.

00:15:33.840 --> 00:15:37.422
That's just like what happened. Sorry.

00:15:37.422 --> 00:15:40.980
(cheerful music)

00:15:40.980 --> 00:15:43.980
Even after the British
people here on the east coast

00:15:43.980 --> 00:15:46.590
of North America wanted
to break away from England

00:15:46.590 --> 00:15:48.397
and start their own country where, quote,

00:15:48.397 --> 00:15:50.040
"All men are created equal,"

00:15:50.040 --> 00:15:54.270
they still couldn't throw
off the thirst for profits

00:15:54.270 --> 00:15:55.470
that slavery brought them.

00:15:55.470 --> 00:15:59.130
These structures were way too
firm, so they kept doing it.

00:15:59.130 --> 00:16:02.640
The momentum of private empire
was too great to slow down,

00:16:02.640 --> 00:16:04.980
at least not without a bloody war

00:16:04.980 --> 00:16:07.393
that almost ripped this
young nation apart.

00:16:07.393 --> 00:16:08.798
(cheerful music)

00:16:08.798 --> 00:16:10.447
(cannons banging)

00:16:10.447 --> 00:16:11.610
(swords clinking)

00:16:11.610 --> 00:16:13.470
So that's private empire,

00:16:13.470 --> 00:16:18.470
a huge part of Europe's ability
to take over land on the map

00:16:18.840 --> 00:16:20.040
and reshape the world.

00:16:20.040 --> 00:16:21.420
In part three of this series,

00:16:21.420 --> 00:16:22.530
which is gonna be the final part,

00:16:22.530 --> 00:16:23.910
I'm gonna tell you what happens next

00:16:23.910 --> 00:16:26.670
when these powers reach
every part of the globe,

00:16:26.670 --> 00:16:29.700
establishing an order that they control,

00:16:29.700 --> 00:16:32.430
how we talk, how we do our
politics, how we trade,

00:16:32.430 --> 00:16:35.280
including some really
good, positive things

00:16:35.280 --> 00:16:36.990
that have made the world better.

00:16:36.990 --> 00:16:38.880
It's an order that was shaped

00:16:38.880 --> 00:16:42.150
by these forces of European imperialism,

00:16:42.150 --> 00:16:45.626
and it's an order that still
shapes all of us today.

00:16:45.626 --> 00:16:48.376
(cheerful music)

